# Gallery thumbnail regen

Whenever a change **visually affects** a visualization (look, framing, color, trail, shader, default params, or new active route), regenerate that slug’s gallery thumb before considering the work done.

## Command

```bash
cd packages/frontend && FRONTEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5173/chaos pnpm thumbs -- --slug <slug>
```

- Requires Vite (`p dev`) on **5173** and air serving icons on **8080**.
- Output: `packages/backend/static/images/<slug>.png`
- Include the new PNG in the same commit/PR as the viz change.

## Triggers (do regen)

- Page under `packages/frontend/src/pages/{attractors,maps,fractals,misc}/`
- Related util/shader that changes the drawn result
- Default camera / scale / color / draw mode / `numParticles`
- Activating or adding a catalog slug in `packages/shared/routes.json`

## Skip

- Copy-only About/docs with no visual change
- Pure infra (proxy, board scripts, OpenSpec text) with no on-canvas difference

## Multi-slug

If several viz changed: regen each affected slug (or full `pnpm thumbs` if many).
